<!--
  Iron Rain (suggestion 2.6): the Society and the Rim Dominion come down from orbit.

  No C# needed after all. Decompiled, PawnsArrivalModeWorker.GetSelectionWeight
  checks the mode's selectionWeightCurvesPerFaction for the raiding faction FIRST and
  only falls back to the general curve when there is no entry - vanilla uses exactly
  this for mechanoids (Core/Defs/Misc/PawnsArrivalModeDefs/PawnsArrivalModes.xml).
  So each arrival mode gets an entry for our two spacefaring powers: drops several
  times likelier than vanilla gives anyone (a centre drop at 1000 points weighs 5.0
  against vanilla's 3.5, a walk-in 0.12 against 0.4), so an Iron Rain on top of the
  colony is the expected way the Society arrives.

  The tribes need nothing: every drop mode has minTechLevel Industrial and the
  Obsidian tribes are Neolithic. The Ascomanni, the Sons of Ares and the merchant
  houses keep vanilla's weights. success Always: a mod that rewrites an arrival mode
  should not take this file down with it.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <success>Always</success>
    <xpath>Defs/PawnsArrivalModeDef[defName="EdgeWalkIn"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <selectionWeightCurvesPerFaction>
          <li>
            <faction>RR_Society</faction>
            <selectionWeightPerPointsCurve>
              <points>
                <li>(300, 0.35)</li>
                <li>(700, 0.12)</li>
              </points>
            </selectionWeightPerPointsCurve>
          </li>
          <li>
            <faction>RR_RimDominion</faction>
            <selectionWeightPerPointsCurve>
              <points>
                <li>(300, 0.35)</li>
                <li>(700, 0.12)</li>
              </points>
            </selectionWeightPerPointsCurve>
          </li>
      </selectionWeightCurvesPerFaction>
    </value>
  </Operation>

